WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.468 --> 00:00:22.094
The that Eponine had delivered was addressed to Marius at 16 Rue de la Verrerie.

2
00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:29.416
He broke the seal and read it: My beloved, Alas, my father wishes us to leave immediately.

3
00:00:30.164 --> 00:00:32.845
Tonight we will stay at 7 Rue de l'Homme Armé.

4
00:00:33.446 --> 00:00:34.826
In a week we will be in England.

5
00:00:35.527 --> 00:00:40.449
Cosette Marius was unaware of how Eponine had come to have this letter.

6
00:00:41.289 --> 00:00:44.711
She had been as much in love with Marius as he was with Cosette.

7
00:00:45.591 --> 00:00:52.394
Determined to keep Marius and Cosette apart, Eponine had borrowed clothes from a young man and warned Valjean

8
00:00:52.474 --> 00:00:53.095
to move out.

9
00:00:54.055 --> 00:01:00.306
After receiving the mysterious warning, Valjean had immediately announced to Cosette and Toussaint that they were leaving.

10
00:01:01.087 --> 00:01:04.709
Cosette needed to write to Marius, but she couldn't take the letter herself.

11
00:01:05.489 --> 00:01:10.632
Fortunately she noticed the young man in velvet trousers loitering outside the garden gate.

12
00:01:11.852 --> 00:01:15.734
Cosette gave the letter to "him," but Eponine did not deliver it.

13
00:01:16.775 --> 00:01:19.756
Now Marius covered Cosette's letter with kisses.

14
00:01:20.397 --> 00:01:21.537
She still loved him!

15
00:01:22.058 --> 00:01:24.519
For a moment it seemed that he did not have to die.

16
00:01:25.099 --> 00:01:26.120
But then he remembered.

17
00:01:27.072 --> 00:01:33.035
"Her father is taking her to England, and my grandfather refuses to consent to our marriage," said Marius

18
00:01:33.075 --> 00:01:33.636
to himself.

19
00:01:34.336 --> 00:01:35.357
"Nothing has changed."

20
00:01:36.557 --> 00:01:38.398
So he had only two duties left.

21
00:01:38.979 --> 00:01:43.781
The first was to write to Cosette one last time and inform her of his certain death.

22
00:01:44.822 --> 00:01:50.245
The second duty was to save Eponine's brother, Gavroche, by getting him away from the barricade.

23
00:01:51.226 --> 00:01:53.527
Marius took a pencil and paper from his pocket.

24
00:01:54.427 --> 00:01:57.436
My dear Cosette: We cannot be married.

25
00:01:58.137 --> 00:02:02.818
I have asked my grandfather for permission, and he has refused me as you and I are both

26
00:02:02.918 --> 00:02:07.859
poor. I ran to your house in the Rue Plumet, but did not find you there.

27
00:02:08.439 --> 00:02:11.100
Do you remember my promise that I would die if you went away?

28
00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:13.981
I will keep it, and I will die.

29
00:02:14.521 --> 00:02:15.081
I love you.

30
00:02:15.501 --> 00:02:19.642
When you read this, my soul will be near you and will smile upon you.

31
00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:27.448
Marius He did not have an envelope, so he merely folded the letter and wrote Cosette's address upon

32
00:02:27.528 --> 00:02:30.749
it. Marius stood lost in thought for a moment.

33
00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:36.051
Then he took out another piece of paper and wrote: My name is Marius Pontmercy.

34
00:02:36.631 --> 00:02:43.013
Carry my corpse to my grandfather's house: Monsieur Gillenormand, 6 Rue des Filles du Calvaire.

35
00:02:43.993 --> 00:02:48.294
He put this note in his pocket, and then he called Eponine's brother, Gavroche.

36
00:02:48.314 --> 00:02:50.475
"Will you do something for me?"

37
00:02:50.995 --> 00:02:51.735
asked Marius.

38
00:02:51.755 --> 00:02:53.515
"Of course I will.

39
00:02:53.976 --> 00:02:55.076
You saved my life."

40
00:02:56.648 --> 00:02:58.269
"Leave the barricade immediately.

41
00:02:58.789 --> 00:03:04.631
Then take this letter first thing tomorrow morning to Mademoiselle Cosette at 7 Rue de l'Homme Armé."

42
00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:08.733
"But I want to be here when the soldiers attack the barricade again.

43
00:03:09.233 --> 00:03:10.654
Can't I leave tomorrow morning?"

44
00:03:10.674 --> 00:03:12.815
"No, it'll be too late.

45
00:03:13.375 --> 00:03:15.736
The streets will be blockaded and you won't be able to get out.

46
00:03:16.356 --> 00:03:17.256
Go right away!"

47
00:03:18.017 --> 00:03:21.718
Gavroche was still puzzled, but he took the letter and scampered away.

48
00:03:21.738 --> 00:03:25.960
"That street is not far away," said Gavroche to himself.

49
00:03:26.584 --> 00:03:29.686
"I can deliver the letter and return in time for the action."

50
00:03:30.586 --> 00:03:35.329
Meanwhile Jean Valjean had calmed down as soon as he reached the Rue de l'Homme Armé.

51
00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:39.091
Cosette had not left the Rue Plumet without resistance.

52
00:03:39.651 --> 00:03:42.593
It was the first time that her will had clashed with his.

53
00:03:44.194 --> 00:03:46.455
They arrived at their new home without speaking.

54
00:03:47.056 --> 00:03:53.099
Valjean was so anxious that he didn't notice Cosette's sadness, and she was so sad that she didn't

55
00:03:53.159 --> 00:03:54.460
perceive his anxiety.

56
00:03:55.304 --> 00:04:00.789
In their flight from the Rue Plumet, Valjean had taken only a small bundle of clothes and the

57
00:04:00.849 --> 00:04:02.710
small suitcase he carried everywhere.

58
00:04:03.591 --> 00:04:08.195
A trunk would have required the help of another man, and another man might talk.

59
00:04:08.775 --> 00:04:11.958
Toussaint and Cosette took a few clothes and toilet articles.

60
00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:15.841
Cosette also took her portable writing desk and its blotter.

61
00:04:16.902 --> 00:04:21.046
The next morning Cosette said that she had a headache and spent the day in bed.

62
00:04:21.686 --> 00:04:25.293
Toward evening she came downstairs, but soon returned to her room.

63
00:04:26.194 --> 00:04:31.057
While Valjean ate a small supper, he became aware that Toussaint was agitated.

64
00:04:31.997 --> 00:04:32.718
"What's wrong?"

65
00:04:33.118 --> 00:04:34.779
he finally asked the old servant.

66
00:04:34.799 --> 00:04:38.961
"I'm not sure what's going on," she said.

67
00:04:38.982 --> 00:04:42.804
"But there seems to be a battle taking place in the city."

68
00:04:42.824 --> 00:04:44.265
"Oh, really?"

69
00:04:44.525 --> 00:04:47.327
he said absently, more concerned with his own affairs.

70
00:04:48.427 --> 00:04:54.219
After supper he felt better and walked around the dining room, still filled with the bundles that Toussaint

71
00:04:54.259 --> 00:04:55.100
had packed for them.

72
00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:57.922
Suddenly he spotted something strange.

73
00:04:58.482 --> 00:05:02.165
Cosette had left her writing desk and blotter on the sideboard when she arrived.

74
00:05:02.985 --> 00:05:08.149
The blotter was reflected in the sideboard's mirror; he could now read the last letter that she had

75
00:05:08.169 --> 00:05:10.851
blotted. It was the letter to Marius.

76
00:05:12.112 --> 00:05:13.232
Valjean was stunned.

77
00:05:13.813 --> 00:05:18.176
Cosette was in love with a man, and she had told him about their move to England.

78
00:05:19.112 --> 00:05:20.433
"She plans to leave me!"

79
00:05:20.893 --> 00:05:21.794
Valjean whispered.

80
00:05:22.274 --> 00:05:23.935
But who could this young man be?

81
00:05:23.955 --> 00:05:29.798
It did not take Valjean long to realize that it must be the one from the Luxembourg Gardens.

82
00:05:30.539 --> 00:05:33.700
There was no other man with whom Cosette had been in contact.

83
00:05:34.561 --> 00:05:37.923
Valjean was so upset that he did not know what he was doing.

84
00:05:38.683 --> 00:05:40.604
He went outside and sat on the steps.

85
00:05:41.805 --> 00:05:46.367
That is what he was doing when Gavroche approached him and asked, "Can you tell me where number

86
00:05:46.427 --> 00:05:47.008
seven is?"

87
00:05:48.128 --> 00:05:49.369
"What do you want with that house?"

88
00:05:49.889 --> 00:05:50.590
asked Valjean.

89
00:05:51.170 --> 00:05:56.454
Gavroche hesitated, but Valjean suddenly had an idea of why the boy might be there.

90
00:05:56.474 --> 00:05:59.516
"Have you brought the letter I'm waiting for?"

91
00:06:00.197 --> 00:06:01.417
"It's not for you.

92
00:06:02.058 --> 00:06:02.939
It's for a woman."

93
00:06:02.959 --> 00:06:06.261
"The letter is for Mademoiselle Cosette, isn't it?

94
00:06:06.901 --> 00:06:08.542
She told me to wait here for it."

95
00:06:08.562 --> 00:06:12.065
"Yes." Gavroche handed over the letter.

96
00:06:12.085 --> 00:06:17.816
"Tell her it came from the barricade at the Rue de la Chanvrerie."

97
00:06:17.836 --> 00:06:23.321
Valjean's heart was filled with malice toward Marius; he wanted to kill his daughter's suitor!

98
00:06:23.902 --> 00:06:27.084
The old man waited until he was inside the house to read the letter.

99
00:06:28.225 --> 00:06:30.647
As he read it, his anger turned to joy.

100
00:06:31.208 --> 00:06:35.451
There was no need to commit murder because Marius was probably already dead.

101
00:06:36.012 --> 00:06:38.294
Cosette would not leave Valjean after all!

102
00:06:39.315 --> 00:06:42.357
And yet Valjean was also filled with gloom.

103
00:06:42.918 --> 00:06:45.440
Cosette would never know what had happened to Marius.

104
00:06:46.048 --> 00:06:49.811
Valjean must try to save him if only for her sake.

105
00:06:50.872 --> 00:06:54.614
For many years Valjean had served as a member of the National Guard.

106
00:06:55.115 --> 00:06:58.417
Before dawn he went out, armed and in his uniform.

107
00:06:59.378 --> 00:07:05.663
Meanwhile Marius had given his role as leader of the rebels to Enjolras, who ordered that the dead

108
00:07:05.723 --> 00:07:06.403
be removed.

109
00:07:07.464 --> 00:07:12.508
Four National Guards had been killed; Enjolras had their uniforms laid aside in a pile.

110
00:07:13.704 --> 00:07:15.945
There were 37 rebels still alive.

111
00:07:16.925 --> 00:07:18.845
Enjolras went out on a scouting mission.

112
00:07:19.526 --> 00:07:22.086
When he returned, he had grim news.

113
00:07:22.106 --> 00:07:25.487
"A third of the army is advancing toward us.

114
00:07:26.267 --> 00:07:28.928
As for the people, they have abandoned us.

115
00:07:29.968 --> 00:07:33.810
We have four National Guard uniforms here, so four of you can escape.

116
00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:36.310
There's no need for everyone to die."

117
00:07:37.230 --> 00:07:39.171
No one wanted to leave the barricade.

118
00:07:39.731 --> 00:07:42.632
It was finally decided that those with families should go.

119
00:07:43.284 --> 00:07:45.867
But that meant five men now wanted to leave.

120
00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:53.837
Marius looked up and saw Cosette's father entering the barricade, dressed in his National Guard uniform.
